[McpTool( "capture", "Screenshots and ground-truth perception captures. 'shot' IS THE SCREENSHOT COMMAND and the only one you should normally need: `capture action=shot target=<what you want to see>` writes a PNG to <repo>/.screenshots/, returns its absolute path, picks the route itself, and proves your subject is in the frame (BINDING contract: docs/ai/contracts/screenshot.md). In play mode it copies the real composited frame, so GPU particles, bloom and post-FX are all present and `blind_to` is empty; in edit mode it re-renders, which can frame any target but cannot show SceneCustomObject draws — read `blind_to` on the result before calling a missing subject a bug. Every other action below is an implementation detail of shot and is gated. 'annotated' (v1): single shot from any pose + manifest. 'orbit_set' (v2.3; token-efficient v2 as of 2026-07-15): multi-pose batch (6-ortho + 8-orbit + top/front/hero/macro views of a target bbox) giving stereoscopic 3D understanding in one round-trip. By DEFAULT (return=montage) it composites every pose into ONE contact-sheet image block — all angles for roughly one image's worth of tokens, instead of the old ~18 inlined base64 strings. Use return=disk (writes per-pose JPEGs to .mcp-capture-sets/<stamp>/ and returns file paths; zero image tokens), return=inline (up to 4 key poses as image blocks), or return=stats (byte accounting, no pixels) as needed. 'channels' (v3.2): per-channel render-pass breakdown — v1 ships an entity_id channel as a synthetic PNG (deterministic-colour rect per visible entity_id + id_legend) plus an 'unavailable' list for the v2-deferred channels (albedo, depth, emissive, normal, specular, motion, roughness). 'baseline_set' / 'baseline_list' / 'diff_baseline' (v4.2): visual regression-catch — store a labelled baseline render at a pose, then compare a fresh render at the same pose against it, returning per-tile luminance delta heatmap + verdict (match / drift / regression) + classification (global-shift / regional-shift / mixed). Baselines are in-memory (process-scoped, cleared on plugin hot-reload), max 32 stored." )]
